    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n34926" root="فيح" body-key="f">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَيَّاحٌ</span></b> : see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَفْيَحُ</span>, in two places. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  Also (tropical:)  <i>Profuse in bounty:</i> (S, A:) so in the saying, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">إِنَّهُ</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَجَوَادٌ فِيَّاحٌ</span> (tropical:)  [<i>Verily he is liberal, munificent,</i> or
<i>generous; profuse in bounty</i>]. (S.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَاقَةٌ</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَيَّاحَةٌ</span> (tropical:)  <i>A she-camel that yields much milk,</i> (A,
K,) <i>and has a large udder.</i> (K.)

